error does not restore progress.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"b7e0a0828e794c5fa40df351cb813d8f-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The entry loop returns on a GetLog error for entries at or below the cached last index, before reaching StoreLogs.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Before the restart (index 9, and still true after the fault was removed at index 10) the wedged node shows exactly the state the earlier receipts recorded: store last index 2 while the certificate is (4,2), GetLog of the certificate index returns 'log not found', the StoreLogs attempt counter is 3 and does not move for the whole 1500 ms window even though the leader's certificate and store hold 1..5, and commit and applied stay at 2. The leader is unchanged at term 3 with commit 5, so the wedge is not a leader-side artefact. After the restart (index 11) the node is rebuilt on the same log store, stable store and snapshot store with a new transport at the same address: the certificate index samples move from 2 to 5 and the store's last index moves from 2 to 5, the commit index moves from 0 to 5, applied reaches 5, the certificate is (5,3) with GetLog of that index succeeding, and the store's attempt/delivery counters advance from 3/2 to 5/4, so the leader's re-sent entries were stored. Convergence happened about 1.8 s after the restart (sample 9 of 20 at 200 ms), which matches the in-memory transport's 500 ms RPC timeout plus backoff for the call that was in flight when Shutdown closed the old transport, and the peers had to be rewired to the new transport because Shutdown closes the transport it was built with. Interpretation of the comparison: the predicate 'a process restart over the same durable state repairs the replica' holds, and 'the running replica repairs itself once the store error stops' does not, which is what the earlier source-derived boundary predicted. This closes the earlier limitation that no restart had been executed; it does not change the wedge defect, which stays asserted for the conditions recorded in the earlier receipts.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The restart repairs the state, so the wedge is not permanent in the presence of an operator restart; the defect's harm is bounded by the operational repair, and this receipt is evidence for the repair rather than for the harm.\\\",\n   \\\"Convergence after the restart took about 1.8 s here, but that duration is a property of the harness (in-memory transport timeout plus the leader's retry backoff after the transport was closed by Shutdown), so it is not a recovery-time claim for real deployments.\\\",\n   \\\"The observation window after the restart was four seconds and the state was consistent from the ninth sample on; no longer-running behaviour is claimed.\\\",\n   \\\"The restart was performed by the harness with the library's own constructor, not by an external process manager, so the modelled restart differs from a real process death in that the same store object was reused rather than reopened from disk.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"One retained execution with deterministic fault injection, three voters, in-memory transport, short timeouts and a hand-modelled restart (fresh transport at the same address, NewRaft over the same stores).\\\",\n   \\\"InstallSnapshot, the other source-derived repair path, was still not executed, and no leader-side compaction was reached, so the set of repairs is confirmed only for the restart path.\\\",\n   \\\"The wedge evidence itself lives in the earlier receipts; this receipt re-witnesses it (indices 5, 6, 9, 10) under the same staging, and the joint history is the same harness lineage with the restart subtest added.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"This receipt comes from the same harness file, with the same staging and the same fault wrapper as the earlier wedge receipts, extended by a third subtest that restarts the node; its control and faulted subtests re-witness the same histories on a fresh process (indices 1, 2, 5, 6, 9, 10 correspond to the earlier receipts' truncation and disarm phases), and its sampling is independent of the earlier receipts.\\\",\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"卡死副本的修复边界已被执行验证：运行中的副本不会自愈，同盘重启可以\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"针对第二条发现（截断窗口内一次合法 StoreLogs 错误会永久卡死该跟随者）此前遗留的『未执行重启/快照修复路径』限制，本次保留执行 \\\"+R+\\\" 补上了边界证据：注入错误后，运行中的副本在 1500 毫秒窗口内以及移除故障后再等 1200 毫秒都无任何进展（store last 仍为 2、证书仍为 (4,2)、对证书下标的 GetLog 报 log not found、StoreLogs 尝试次数停在 3、commit/applied 停在 2，而领导者侧为 1..5、commit 5）；随后在同一份持久状态（同一 log store/stable store/snapshot store，同地址新 transport，Shutdown 会关闭旧 transport，故对端需重新接线）上重启该节点后，证书与存储在下标 2→5、commit 0→5，最终证书 (5,3)、GetLog 成功、StoreLogs 计数 3/2→5/4，即重启修复成功。结论：该缺陷的修复边界得到执行确认——运行中的副本不会自愈，同盘重启可以；约 1.8 秒的恢复延迟是本地测试设施（500 毫秒 RPC 超时 + 重试退避）的产物，不作为生产恢复时间。缺陷主张维持不变，InstallSnapshot 路径仍未执行。\\\"\n }],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@restart-repairs-wedge-not-selfheal\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\":\\\"A wedged replica (conflict-truncation store-error state) does not converge while running, even after the store error is removed, but a restart over the same durable state does converge: after restarting the same stores with a fresh transport at the same address, the certificate, the store's last index and the commit index return to the leader's values and the leader's re-sent entries are stored (certificate (5,3) versus the wedged (4,2), commit 0 to 5).\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Three-voter cluster, in-memory transport, the store wrapper's error no longer injected; restart modelled as NewRaft over the same log store, stable store and snapshot store with a new transport at the same address and the peers rewired (Shutdown closes the transport it was built with). Observed for four seconds after the restart with 200 ms sampling.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"appendentries-conflict-truncate-block\\\",\\\"appendentries-store-failure-todo\\\",\\\"appendentries-entry-loop-cached-lastlog\\\",\\\"replication-nextindex-floor\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{R:[11,10,9,6,5]}}\n ]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(upd,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nprint('ok', json.load(open('update.json'))['interpretations'][0]['conclusion'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"ok holds\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
